# info_test_module.pal - PHASE 2 per-screen module split (2026-07-31,
# #.haiku+/!.xyzos-standards+1.txt §41), proven first in 01.muchi-
# pals-🥚️-13.01, now applied here. pieces/chtpm/layouts/info_test.chtpm's
# own DEDICATED module - game.chtpm and info_test.chtpm used to both
# resolve to the SAME project-wide ${module_path} variable (confirmed:
# pieces/apps/player_app/state.txt's own module_path=system/prisc+x
# pal/main_loop_chtpm.pal, identical for the whole project regardless
# of layout) - each now gets its own distinct, literal module string,
# so chtpm_parser_pal.c's real launch_module() liveness check (kill+
# relaunch on genuine navigation, reuse while staying on one screen)
# applies per screen. Identical CONTENT to the original main_loop_
# chtpm.pal on purpose (including for info_test.chtpm - the real game
# world/monsters keep simulating via game_dispatch's own end_turn/
# tick_monsters even while viewing the info screen, matching original
# behavior exactly) - only the FILENAME differs, which is all launch_
# module()'s own strcmp() actually compares.
li x1, 0

compose_frame
compose_rgb_frame
hit_frame

loop:
exec ./ops/+x/game_dispatch
sleep 16667
j loop
